# L §7.1 (round 12): "pow(x, n) with an integer n is exact; where x has a unit, n is a literal, so the result's unit is
# known at load (LOAD-UNIT otherwise)". (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §7.1, writer 5's T-98.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input n: int
input x: money PLN
def a: num PLN = pow(x, n)
ask q: a
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT pow of money PLN to a power that is not a literal (m.tally:11)
